# Plugins

## Process model

- Separate binary/container per plugin; lifecycle independent of core monolith.
- Core talks **gRPC** via Plugin Manager; frontend via **iframe/WebView + postMessage**.

## Manifest

- Declare name, version, permission scopes upfront; admin approval at install (SDD §6.8).
- Register plugin permissions in catalog (`source_plugin_id`) — align with RBAC §6.2.

## Boundaries

- Workspace plugins: server + shared UI tab/sidebar.
- Client-only plugins: no server trust; never send workspace secrets to personal plugins.

Virtual Office and heavy spatial features stay plugins — core must run fine without them.
